#: ../../../platforms.rst:7
msgid "Cross-platform xonsh RC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:9
msgid ""
"First of all because a :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` is plain xonsh code, you "
"can ship a single file across Linux, macOS, and Windows and gate snippets on "
"platform and execution-mode flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:13
msgid "Platform flags are lazy booleans exposed by :mod:`xonsh.platform`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:15
msgid "``ON_LINUX`` — Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:16
msgid "``ON_DARWIN`` — macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:17
msgid "``ON_WINDOWS`` — native Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:18
msgid ""
"``ON_POSIX``, ``ON_CYGWIN``, ``ON_MSYS``, ``ON_FREEBSD``, ``ON_NETBSD``, "
"``ON_OPENBSD``, ``ON_DRAGONFLY``, ``ON_BSD`` (any of the four) — other OS "
"families"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:21
msgid ""
"``ON_ANDROID`` — any Android userland: Termux, UserLAnd, proot-distro, Linux "
"Deploy chroot, and so on. Note that ``ON_LINUX`` is **False** on Android "
"with Python 3.13+ (see PEP 738), so gate Android-aware code on "
"``ON_ANDROID`` rather than ``ON_LINUX``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:25
msgid ""
"``ON_TERMUX`` — specifically the Termux app (and forks that keep its "
"``$TERMUX_VERSION`` env var). Implies ``ON_ANDROID`` plus the Termux "
"``$PREFIX = /data/data/com.termux/files/usr`` userland layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:28
msgid "``IN_APPIMAGE`` — running inside an AppImage bundle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:29
msgid "``IN_FLATPAK`` — running inside a Flatpak sandbox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:31
msgid "Execution-mode flags live in the environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:33
msgid ""
"``$XONSH_INTERACTIVE`` — ``True`` when xonsh is running an interactive "
"shell. Use it to gate anything that only makes sense with a live terminal "
"(aliases you type, key bindings, prompt colors, xontribs that hook the "
"REPL). Safe to use inside an RC that is ``source``-d at runtime, because it "
"reflects the current session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:38
msgid ""
"``$XONSH_MODE`` — the startup mode as a string: ``interactive``, "
"``script_from_file``, ``source``, ``single_command``, ``script_from_stdin``. "
"Useful to distinguish \"started as a shell\" from \"invoked to run one "
"command\" or \"executed as a script\". For gating logic inside an RC, prefer "
"``$XONSH_INTERACTIVE`` — ``$XONSH_MODE`` reflects the original startup mode, "
"not the context the RC is currently running in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:45
msgid "Typical pattern:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:47
msgid ""
"from xonsh.platform import ON_LINUX, ON_DARWIN, ON_WINDOWS\n"
"\n"
"if $XONSH_INTERACTIVE:\n"
"    # Only in a live terminal — skipped when the RC is run as a script\n"
"    aliases['ll'] = 'ls -la'\n"
"    $PROMPT = $PROMPT.replace('{prompt_end}', 'myproject {prompt_end}')\n"
"\n"
"    if ON_LINUX:\n"
"        $LS_COLORS = 'di=1;34:ln=35'\n"
"    elif ON_DARWIN:\n"
"        aliases['ls'] = 'ls -G'\n"
"    elif ON_WINDOWS:\n"
"        $PATHEXT.append('.PY')\n"
"else:\n"
"    # Script / non-interactive mode — fail fast\n"
"    $XONSH_SHOW_TRACEBACK = True\n"
"    $XONSH_SUBPROC_CMD_RAISE_ERROR = True"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:68
msgid "\\*nix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:70
msgid ""
"Tips that apply to Unix-like systems in general (Linux, macOS, BSD, WSL). "
"Platform-specific notes live in their own sections below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:74 ../../../platforms.rst:348
msgid "Tab completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:76
msgid ""
"Xonsh has support for using bash completion files on the shell. To use it "
"you need to install the bash-completion package. The regular bash-completion "
"package uses v1 which mostly works, but we recommend using `bash-completion "
"v2 <https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh/issues/2111>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:81
msgid ""
"Bash completion comes from the `bash-completion project <https://github.com/"
"scop/bash-completion>`_ which suggests you use a package manager to install "
"it. The package manager will also install a new version of bash without "
"affecting ``/bin/bash``. Xonsh also needs to be told where the bash "
"completion file is — add it to ``$BASH_COMPLETIONS``. The package includes "
"completions for many Unix commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:89
msgid "Common packaging systems for macOS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:91
msgid "**Homebrew** — install the ``bash-completion2`` package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:93
msgid "@ brew install bash-completion2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:97
msgid ""
"This will install the completion file to ``/usr/local/share/bash-completion/"
"bash_completion`` (Intel Mac) or ``/opt/homebrew/share/bash-completion/"
"bash_completion`` (Apple Silicon) — both are in the default xonsh search "
"path and should just work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:102
msgid ""
"**MacPorts** — install the ``bash-completion`` port (`docs <https://trac."
"macports.org/wiki/howto/bash-completion>`_):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:105
msgid "@ sudo port install bash-completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:109
msgid ""
"This includes a completion file that needs to be added to the environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:111
msgid ""
"@ $BASH_COMPLETIONS.insert(0, '/opt/local/share/bash-completion/"
"bash_completion')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:116
msgid ""
"The `bash-completion project page <https://github.com/scop/bash-"
"completion>`_ refers to ``.../profile.d/bash_completion.sh`` which in turn "
"sources the main completion script mentioned above and one in "
"``$XDG_CONFIG_HOME``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:120
msgid ""
"Alternatively, take a look at `xontrib-fish-completer <https://github.com/"
"xonsh/xontrib-fish-completer>`_ for a modern fish-style approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:126
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:129
msgid "Colored man pages"
