msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:171
msgid "UTF-8 characters and locale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:173
msgid "If UTF-8 characters fail with errors like::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:175
msgid ""
"@ echo \"ßðđ\"\n"
"UnicodeEncodeError: 'ascii' codec can't encode characters in position 0-2..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:178
msgid ""
"your process locale is not UTF-8. Usually seen in minimal containers, "
"stripped SSH sessions, systemd units, or cron jobs where ``LANG`` / "
"``LC_ALL`` are set to ``C`` or ``POSIX``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:182
msgid ""
"The locale must be set **before** xonsh starts — setting ``$LC_ALL`` from "
"your :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` is too late for subprocesses that already "
"inherited the broken environment. Fix it at the OS level (``~/."
"pam_environment``, ``/etc/locale.conf``, the container image's base layer, "
"or the systemd unit's ``Environment=`` directive). As a temporary "
"workaround, ``PYTHONUTF8=1`` forces Python into UTF-8 mode regardless of "
"locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:190
msgid "Bash module warnings on startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:192
msgid ""
"Depending on how your installation of Bash is configured, xonsh may show "
"warnings when loading certain shell modules. If you see errors similar to "
"this when launching xonsh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:196
msgid ""
"bash: module: line 1: syntax error: unexpected end of file\n"
"bash: error importing function definition for 'BASH_FUNC_module'\n"
"bash: scl: line 1: syntax error: unexpected end of file\n"
"bash: error importing function definition for 'BASH_FUNC_scl'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:203
msgid "Unset the affected functions in your ``~/.bashrc``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:205
msgid ""
"$ unset module\n"
"$ unset scl"
msgstr ""

