#: ../../../platforms.rst:482
msgid "How to add xonsh into the context menu for Windows?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:484
msgid ""
"In Windows, there's a context menu support for opening a folder in a shell, "
"such as `Open PowerShell window here`. You might want to have a similar menu "
"that opens a folder in xonsh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:486
msgid "context_menu_windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:491
msgid ""
"Usually it involves modifying registry to get it, but `a contributed script "
"<https://gist.github.com/nedsociety/91041691d0ac18bc8fd9e937ad21b055>`_ can "
"be used for automating chores for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:493
msgid ""
"# Open xonsh and copy-paste the following line:\n"
"@ exec(@.imp.urllib.request.urlopen(r'https://gist.githubusercontent.com/"
"nedsociety/91041691d0ac18bc8fd9e937ad21b055/raw/xonsh_context_menu.py')."
"read()) \\\n"
"   && xonsh_register_right_click()\n"
"\n"
"# To remove the menu, use following line instead:\n"
"@ exec(@.imp.urllib.request.urlopen(r'https://gist.githubusercontent.com/"
"nedsociety/91041691d0ac18bc8fd9e937ad21b055/raw/xonsh_context_menu.py')."
"read()) \\\n"
"   && xonsh_unregister_right_click()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:505
msgid "Nice colors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:507
msgid "The dark red and blue colors are completely unreadable in `cmd.exe`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:509
msgid "intensify-colors-win-false"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:514
msgid ""
"Xonsh has some tricks to fix colors. This is controlled by the :ref:"
"`$INTENSIFY_COLORS_ON_WIN <intensify_colors_on_win>` environment variable "
"which is ``True`` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:519
msgid ""
":ref:`$INTENSIFY_COLORS_ON_WIN <intensify_colors_on_win>` has the following "
"effect:b"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:521
msgid "On Windows 10:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:522
msgid ""
"Windows 10 supports true color in the terminal, so on Windows 10 Xonsh will "
"use a style with hard coded colors instead of the terminal colors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:525
msgid "On older Windows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:526
msgid ""
"Xonsh replaces some of the unreadable dark colors with more readable "
"alternatives (e.g. blue becomes cyan)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:531
msgid "Avoid locking the working directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:533
msgid ""
"Python (like other processes on Windows) locks the current working directory "
"so it can't be deleted or renamed. ``cmd.exe`` has this behaviour as well, "
"but it is quite annoying for a shell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:537
msgid ""
"The :ref:`free_cwd <free_cwd>` xontrib (add-on) for xonsh solves some of "
"this problem. It works by hooking the prompt to reset the current working "
"directory to the root drive folder whenever the shell is idle. It only works "
"with the prompt-toolkit back-end. To enable that behaviour run the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:542
msgid "@ xpip install xontrib-free-cwd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:546
msgid ""
"Add this line to your :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` to have it always enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:548
msgid "@ xontrib load free_cwd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:554
msgid "Name space shadowing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:556
msgid ""
"Due to ambiguity with the Python ``dir`` builtin, to list the current "
"directory you must explicitly request the ``dir .``, create an alias or set "
"`$XONSH_BUILTINS_TO_CMD <envvars.html#XONSH_BUILTINS_TO_CMD>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:560
msgid ""
"Many people create a ``d`` alias for the ``dir`` command to save typing and "
"avoid the ambiguity altogether:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:563
msgid "@ aliases['d'] = ['cmd', '/c', 'dir']"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:567
msgid ""
"You can add aliases to your :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` to have it always "
"available when xonsh starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:570
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the experimental ``$XONSH_BUILTINS_TO_CMD`` setting makes "
"bare Python builtin names (``dir``, ``zip``, ``type``, etc.) run as "
"subprocess commands when a matching alias or executable exists:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:574
msgid ""
"@ $XONSH_BUILTINS_TO_CMD = True\n"
"@ dir\n"
" Volume in drive C is Windows\n"
" ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:583
msgid "Working Directory on PATH"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:585
msgid ""
"Windows users, particularly those coming from the ``cmd.exe`` shell, might "
"be accustomed to being able to run executables from the current directory by "
"simply typing the program name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:589
msgid ""
"Since version 0.16, ``xonsh`` follows the more secure and modern approach of "
"not including the current working directory in the search path, similar to "
"Powershell and popular Unix shells. To invoke commands in the current "
"directory on any platform, include the current directory explicitly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:595
msgid "@ ./my-program"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:599
msgid ""
"Although not recommended, to restore the behavior found in the ``cmd.exe`` "
"shell, simply append ``.`` to the ``PATH``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:602
msgid "@ $PATH.append('.')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:606
msgid ""
"Add that to your :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` to enable that as the default "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:610
msgid "Updating xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:612
msgid ""
"On Windows the running ``xonsh.exe`` is locked by the OS, so pip cannot "
"replace it from inside xonsh itself. Use :ref:`xcontext <aliases-xcontext>` "
"to find the interpreter path, exit the shell, then run pip from another "
"terminal (``cmd``, PowerShell, or Windows Terminal):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:618
msgid ""
"@ xcontext            # note the \"xpython\" path\n"
"@ exit                # release the lock on xonsh.exe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:623
msgid "> <xpython> -m pip install --upgrade xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:627
msgid ""
"If you installed xonsh via the `WinGet installer <https://github.com/xonsh/"
"xonsh-winget/releases>`_, download the latest installer and run it — it will "
"upgrade in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:631
msgid ""
"See also :ref:`Updating xonsh <updating_xonsh>` in the installation guide "
"for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:636
msgid "Commands Cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:638
msgid ""
"Windows filesystem access can be slow, especially on network drives or "
"directories like ``C:\\Windows\\System32`` with thousands of executables. "
"Xonsh scans ``$PATH`` directories to resolve commands, which may cause "
"noticeable lag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:643
msgid ""
"The ``$XONSH_COMMANDS_CACHE_READ_DIR_ONCE`` variable tells xonsh to cache "
"directory listings on first access and never re-read them within the "
"session. On Windows it defaults to ``C:\\Windows`` (via ``%WINDIR%``), "
"meaning ``C:\\Windows\\System32`` and all other subdirectories are scanned "
"once and cached for the rest of the session. You can extend it with "
"additional slow directories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:650
msgid ""
"@ $XONSH_COMMANDS_CACHE_READ_DIR_ONCE += ['C:\\\\Program Files', 'C:\\"
"\\Program Files (x86)']"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:654
msgid "On WSL, xonsh auto-detects ``/mnt/*/Windows`` directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:656
msgid "To debug command resolution, enable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:658
msgid "@ $XONSH_COMMANDS_CACHE_TRACE = True"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:664
msgid "Drive letter shortcut for path completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:666
msgid ""
"Windows paths are long. You can define a short environment variable for a "
"drive root and use it with tab completion to navigate quickly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:669
msgid ""
"# Simple assignment\n"
"$C = 'c:\\\\'\n"
"\n"
"# Or register with a description\n"
"@.env.register('C', type='str', default='c:\\\\', doc='Drive C root')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:677
msgid ""
"Now ``cd $C\\<Tab>`` expands ``$C`` and completes paths on the ``C:\\`` "
"drive — the same way ``cd ~/`` completes paths in the home directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:680
msgid "To register all drives present on the system at once:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:682
msgid ""
"for letter in @.imp.string.ascii_uppercase:\n"
"    root = f'{letter}:\\\\'\n"
"    if @.imp.os.path.isdir(root):\n"
"        @.env.register(letter, type='str', default=root,\n"
"                       doc=f'Drive {letter} root')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:690
msgid ""
"Add this to your :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` to have drive shortcuts available "
"in every session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:695
msgid "Forward-slash paths (``$FORCE_POSIX_PATHS``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:697
msgid ""
"Set ``$FORCE_POSIX_PATHS = True`` to make xonsh display and complete paths "
"with forward slashes (``/``) instead of backslashes (``\\``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:700
msgid ""
"$FORCE_POSIX_PATHS = True\n"
"cd ~/Documents\n"
"# prompt shows: C:/Users/me/Documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms.rst:706
msgid ""
"Most modern Windows applications accept forward-slash paths, but not all do "
"(notably ``cmd.exe`` does not). In practice Git, Python, VS Code, and many "
"other tools work fine with ``/``."
msgstr ""

